@startuml MagicLinkSSO-Bootstrap-Flow

title Magic Link SSO Application-Owned Browser Sign-In (Bootstrap)
hide footbox

participant "User's browser" as Browser
participant "Application\n(SDK or Gate)" as App
participant "SSO server" as SSO

== Prepare the Application Form ==

Browser -> App: Enter SSO start route
App -> SSO: GET /sso/capabilities (backend)
SSO --> App: Browser SSO + bootstrap capability
App --> Browser: Set encrypted state/PKCE transaction;\nredirect to /sso/authorize?loginUi=app-owned&...
Browser -> SSO: GET /sso/authorize
note over Browser, SSO
An allowed existing central identity takes the normal code/exchange
flow instead. The sequence below starts without a reusable identity.
end note
SSO --> Browser: Set browser binding; redirect to registered\nstart (ssoPrepared=1, state, requestId)
Browser -> App: GET prepared start
App -> SSO: POST /sso/bootstrap/inspect (backend)\nrequestId, codeVerifier, redirectUri
SSO --> App: Validated request context
App --> Browser: Store encrypted continuation; show local form

== Establish the Local Application Session ==

Browser -> App: Submit email
App -> SSO: POST /signin (backend)\nemail, trusted URLs, scope, browserSso context
SSO -> SSO: Check grant; send magic link + optional OTP
ref over Browser, SSO
    Local magic-link preview and explicit confirmation,
    or OTP entry in the application's existing form
end ref
App -> SSO: POST /verify-email or /verify-email/otp\nwith matching browserSso context (backend)
SSO -> SSO: Consume email grant once; issue local JWT;\nissue bootstrap ticket when context is valid
SSO --> App: { accessToken, browserSso: { bootstrapTicket } }\nor valid accessToken with bootstrap failure
App -> App: Verify JWT; bind continuation to its exact hash
App --> Browser: Set local JWT cookie before shared continuation

== Establish the Shared Browser Identity ==

opt Bootstrap ticket available
    Browser -> SSO: Top-level GET /sso/bootstrap/redeem\nticket, redirectUri, state
    opt Different/missing browser binding or different central account
        SSO --> Browser: Show verified account for explicit confirmation
        Browser -> SSO: Confirm; POST /sso/bootstrap/redeem (CSRF)
    end
    SSO -> SSO: Recheck current grants; atomically consume ticket;\nreplace central session
    SSO --> Browser: Set issuer-only central cookie
    alt Original browser binding matches
        SSO --> Browser: Redirect to app callback\nstate, browserSso=complete, HMAC receipt
        Browser -> App: GET registered SSO callback
        App -> App: Require transaction + finish continuation;\nverify existing local JWT, exact hash and receipt
        App --> Browser: Clear transaction/continuation; saved returnUrl
        note right of App
            Finish retains the existing local JWT.
            It sets no authentication cookie
            and performs no second JWT exchange.
        end note
    else Ticket confirmed in another browser
        SSO --> Browser: Offer registered start URI for fresh app state
    end
end

note over Browser, SSO
Missing/expired ticket, denied bootstrap, or a lost result leaves
a valid local JWT usable. Offer app entry and fresh hosted sign-in;
never retry a consumed ticket or email grant.
Central logout cancels outstanding bootstrap tickets.
Later entry into another app uses normal state/PKCE authorization.
end note

@enduml
